c. strengthening and developing service provider institutions for improving family quality in realizing Children's rights;
d. guaranteeing the Protection, care, and welfare of Children with due regard to the rights and obligations of parents, guardians, or other persons who are legally responsible for the Child;
e. providing facilities and infrastructure in the implementation of the fulfillment of Children's rights;
f. guaranteeing the right of Children to express opinions in accordance with the age and level of intelligence of the Child; g. conducting supervision and guidance in the context of implementing the fulfillment of Children's rights; and h. cooperating with the private sector and/or NGOs in the implementation of Child Protection;
2. The responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1) are carried out by Regional Apparatus in accordance with their duties and functions.

Article 31

